<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre was the killing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and other French cities in 1572, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> contrast it with the Commonwealth's tolerance. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw-confederation">Warsaw Confederation</a> of 1573 established legal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/religious-tolerance">religious tolerance</a> at the same time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-bartholomews-day-massacre.jpg" alt="St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Dubois 1529-1584 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_masacre_de_San_Bartolom%C3%A9,_por_Fran%C3%A7ois_Dubois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
